Original issue: getting error to get both strutured and unstructured data with the help of baml

When parsing the response from the LLM for a `BalanceSheet` object, both of the `structured`  `yearsUnstructured` field is returned as `null`, **despite the LLM outputting a full and valid-looking JSON** for it.

This only happens after the full response is streamed — during streaming the values appear correct. Once parsing completes, both `years` and `yearsUnstructured` return empty arrays.

```baml

class BalanceSheet{
  years FinancialYear[]
  yearsUnstructured FinancialYearUnstructured[] @description("Raw extracted data including all discovered fields")
}

class FinancialYear {
  year string
  assets Assets
  liabilities Liabilities
  equity Equity
}

class FinancialYearUnstructured {
  year string
  assetsUnstructured AssetsUnstructured
  liabilitiesunstructured LiabilitiesUnstructured
  equityunstructured EquityUnstructured
}

class Assets {
  total_assets float
  current_assets CurrentAssets
  noncurrent_assets NonCurrentAssets
}

class AssetsUnstructured {
  au string @description("all the assets in json from the balance sheet.This includes all fields found in the document.")
}

class Liabilities {
  total_liabilities float
  current_liabilities CurrentLiabilities
  noncurrent_liablities NonCurrentLiabilities
}

class CurrentLiabilities {
  accounts_payable float?
  total_current_liabilities float?
}

class NonCurrentLiabilities {
  total_noncurrent_liabilities float?
}

class LiabilitiesUnstructured {
  lu string @description("all the liabilities in json from the balance sheet.This includes all fields found in the document.")
}

class CurrentAssets {
  cash_and_cash_equivalents float?
  receivables float?
  inventory float?
  total_current_assets float?
}


class NonCurrentAssets{
  property_and_equipment float?
  other_noncurrent_assets float?
  total_noncurrent_assets float?
}


class Equity {
  capital_stock float?
  deficit float?
  retained_earnings float? 
  additional_paid_in_capital float?
  total_equity float
}

class EquityUnstructured {
  eu string @description("all the equity in json from the balance sheet.This includes all fields found in the document.")
}


function ExtractBalanceSheet(statement_image: image) -> BalanceSheet {
  client "my_llm"
  prompt #"
    You are a financial document analyzer. Extract information from this balance sheet in one json format.:
    1. A structured format matching the predefined schema
    2. An unstructured format that captures ALL fields present in the document, even those not in the schema
    Guidelines:
    - For the structured output, extract only the fields defined in the schema
    - For the unstructured output, extract every financial field you can find, preserving the original names
    - Include all numerical values exactly as they appear
    - Maintain hierarchical relationships between fields
    - Record any additional fields or categories discovered
    - Ensure accuracy in numerical values and classifications
    {{ _.role("user") }}
    Extract complete information from this balance sheet:
    {{ statement_image }}
    {{ ctx.output_format }}
  "#
}
